            <ArticleTitle>Stages of development of traditional simulation unit of surgery for manual extra capsular cataract extraction in sub-Saharan African region.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>261</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.11604/pamj.2017.27.261.10980</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The manual extracapsular extraction of the lens is the surgical technique that is most practiced for the treatment of cataract in sub-Saharan Africa. Learning this technique requires the creation of a surgical simulation unit within training institutes. We describe the development stages of a traditional simulation unit. For this purpose, we present a description of four steps involved in the development of a simulation unit for cataract surgery: the physical creation of the room, the aseptic and antisepsis conditions, the management of the eyes, the development of a curriculum and the administrative policies.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
